[{:frontmatter
  {:id "adr-2607110300-cloud-itonami-lei-corporate-tos-catalog"
   :title "ADR-2607110300: cloud-itonami-lei-<LEI> — per-company Terms-of-Service catalog, LEI-keyed (real listed companies, full-text + provenance)"
   :status "accepted"
   :doc_type "adr"
   :topic "cloud-itonami-lei-corporate-tos-catalog"
   :authoritative true
   :last_verified "2026-07-10"
   :authoritative_for
   ["real major/listed companies' service Terms-of-Service analysis+archival lives under the
     cloud-itonami org, one repo per company, named `cloud-itonami-lei-<LEI code>` (ISO 17442
     Legal Entity Identifier as the collision-proof key)"
    "GTIN is rejected as the per-company key -- ADR-2607031800 already ruled a GTIN identifies one
     product, not a legal entity, and this family hits the exact same mismatch"
    "LEI (ISO 17442) is adopted as the unique key -- matsurigoto's LEI/ISO-7064-MOD-97-10
     implementation (etzhayyim/root) is already ported into cloud-itonami-M6910 (ADR-2607031500),
     giving this workspace an existing, correct 'points at a legal entity' identifier"
    "each repo is a read-only reference/archive actor, not an Advisor-Governor actuation actor --
     it proposes or executes nothing on the company's behalf"
    "ToS is a contract meant for full public reliance, so full-text storage is acceptable, but every
     entry must carry source-url + retrieved-at + sha256 + supersedes-chain (reusing
     ADR-2607072300's git-journal pattern) and the README must disclaim non-affiliation to avoid
     trademark/endorsement confusion"
    "public / AGPL-3.0-or-later / not west-managed / no RAD registration -- matches the existing
     cloud-itonami-isic/isco/gtin blueprint convention (owner decided public this session,
     superseding an earlier private-by-default recommendation)"]
   :related
   ["90-docs/adr/2607031800-cloud-itonami-gtin-functional-blueprints.md"
    "90-docs/adr/2607031500-cloud-itonami-m6910-global-incorporation-actor.md"
    "90-docs/adr/2607072300-actor-public-data-git-journal-kotobase-index.md"
    "90-docs/adr/2607110200-kawaraban-r0-r1-cloud-itonami-isco-3521-media-broadcast.md"
    "manifest/repos.edn"]
   :supersedes []
   :superseded_by []}

  :problem
  {:source "session request 2026-07-10: analyze major companies' services/actors and Terms of
            Service, record as EDN, store in kotobase.net + each GitHub repo, one repo per real
            listed company; which org (etzhayyim/cloud-itonami/kotoba-lang) should host it"
   :investigated
   ["cloud-itonami-{isic,isco,cofog,unspsc}-<code> is a 43+-vertical Open Business Blueprint fleet,
     but keyed by generic industry/occupation classification codes -- none of it names or analyzes a
     specific real company"
    "GTIN was already evaluated for exactly this kind of per-unit keying and rejected
     (ADR-2607031800): a GTIN identifies ONE product with no entity-level hierarchy, so 'one repo
     per company, keyed by GTIN' is incoherent the same way 'one repo per GTIN code' was"
    "LEI (ISO 17442) is already implemented in this workspace: matsurigoto (etzhayyim/root) built
     LEI issuance + ISO 7064 MOD 97-10 check-digit logic, and cloud-itonami-M6910 (ADR-2607031500)
     already ported it verbatim -- LEI is GLEIF's global legal-entity identifier, a correct
     'points at a company' key unlike GTIN"
    "ADR-2607072300 already decided the general actor-public-data shape: git-resident EDN journal
     (80-data/public/*.journal.edn) as source of truth, kotobase.net/kotobase-peer as a derived,
     rebuildable index -- but the kotobase.net ingestion job itself remains unbuilt"
    "ToS content differs from kawaraban's journalism content (headline+link+<=280char excerpt only,
     ADR-2607110200): a ToS is a contract meant for full public reliance, not editorial/creative
     work, so full-text archival carries comparatively lower legal risk -- but not zero, since it
     is still a verbatim copy of a third party's published contract text"]
   :risk "storing full ToS text with no provenance loses the traceability of which version/date a
          given clause came from, and repo naming after a real company's brand risks implying
          affiliation/endorsement if not explicitly disclaimed"}

  :decision
  {:naming
   {:pattern "cloud-itonami-lei-<lei-code-lowercase>, one repo per company"
    :org "cloud-itonami (not etzhayyim: non-profit/self-sovereign religious layer, out of scope for
          commercial competitor analysis; not kotoba-lang: language/infra tooling layer, not a home
          for analyzed business content)"
    :key-source "LEI values must come from GLEIF's official registry -- never fabricated, same
                 discipline as the isic-family spec-basis citations"}
   :actor-nature
   {:shape "read-only reference/archive actor, NOT an Advisor-Governor actuation actor -- proposes
            or executes nothing on the company's behalf; same class as cloud-itonami-gtin-catalog"
    :rad "not RAD-registered -- no agency, same reasoning as cloud-itonami-isco-3521's
          non-registration"
    :west "not west-managed -- standalone repo, matching isic/isco/gtin/M6910 convention"}
   :data-schema
   {:file "80-data/public/tos.journal.edn"
    :format "EDN quad-log [<doc-id> :attr value <tx> :add], reusing ADR-2607072300's journal
              pattern"
    :attrs [":tos/full-text (verbatim, unedited)" ":tos/source-url"
            ":tos/retrieved-at" ":tos/sha256 (checksum for change detection)"
            ":tos/doc-type (:terms-of-service/:privacy-policy/:cookie-policy/etc.)"
            ":tos/supersedes (prior doc-id, forming a revision chain -- ToS-change tracking is
             this catalog's own added value)"]
    :company-identity [":company/legal-name" ":company/lei" ":company/jurisdiction"
                        ":company/website" ":company/ticker (optional, exchange-specific)"]
    :sourcing "all company-identity fields cited from GLEIF/exchange disclosure, never guessed"
    :kotobase-role "unchanged from ADR-2607072300: derived, rebuildable index; ingestion job still
                    not implemented, carried forward as an open item"}
   :licensing-and-attribution
   {:repo-license "AGPL-3.0-or-later, matching existing cloud-itonami convention"
    :notice "a NOTICE file states archived third-party ToS text under 80-data/ remains the source
             company's copyright, included for reference/analysis with source-url+retrieved-at
             provenance, not asserted as this project's own work"
    :disclaimer "README must state up front: independent third-party analysis/archive, not
                 affiliated with or endorsed by the analyzed company"}
   :visibility "public (owner decision this session, overriding an earlier private-by-default
                recommendation; consistent with the existing isic/isco/gtin/M6910 public/AGPL
                convention -- CLAUDE.md's gftdcojp-private default applies to the gftdcojp org
                itself, not to cloud-itonami)"
   :pilot "no pilot company selected in this ADR -- pattern/design only; the first concrete repo
           (LEI lookup -> fetch -> journal -> repo creation -> push) is a follow-up implementation
           step, same deferral ADR-2607072300 itself left open"
   :robotics-premise "false -- pure data/documentation service, same exemption class as
                       cloud-itonami-6310 / cloud-itonami-gtin-*"}

  :consequences
  {:resolves "gives 'one repo per real company' a collision-proof, globally-verifiable key (LEI)
              without reviving the GTIN mismatch ADR-2607031800 already closed"
   :new-value "full-text + source-url/retrieved-at/sha256 provenance turns git history itself into a
               ToS change-tracker, a capability this workspace did not have before"
   :fits-convention "sits inside the existing cloud-itonami-* blueprint conventions (public/AGPL/no
                      west registration/no robotics) rather than inventing a fourth divergent
                      structure"
   :open-gap "kotobase.net ingestion job (journal -> kotobase-peer fold) remains unbuilt, the same
              gap ADR-2607072300 already flagged"
   :residual-legal-risk "lower than kawaraban-style journalism content, but not zero -- this still
                          verbatim-copies a third party's published contract text; mitigated via
                          attribution + non-affiliation disclaimer, not eliminated"
   :unproven "no pilot company chosen yet -- the pattern is unverified until a first real repo is
              built end-to-end"}

  :alternatives
  [{:option "GTIN-keyed (cloud-itonami-gtin-<code>)"
    :rejected_because "ADR-2607031800 already ruled this incoherent: a GTIN identifies one product,
                        not a legal entity"}
   {:option "ticker/exchange-code-keyed"
    :rejected_because "exchange-specific numbering is not globally uniform, and unlisted
                        subsidiaries of listed parents may have no ticker at all, whereas LEI is a
                        single global ISO standard covering any legal entity regardless of listing
                        venue"}
   {:option "kawaraban-style excerpt-only storage"
    :rejected_because "a ToS is a contract whose full text is the compliance-relevant artifact --
                        summarizing would discard the actual clauses this catalog exists to
                        preserve; the copyright calculus differs from editorial/journalism content"}
   {:option "house under etzhayyim or kotoba-lang"
    :rejected_because "etzhayyim is the non-profit/self-sovereign religious layer, out of scope for
                        commercial competitor analysis; kotoba-lang is the language/infra tooling
                        layer, not a home for analyzed business content"}]}]
